{"at":"2026-11-19T04:09:10.937Z","date":"2026-11-21","word":"良好","id":1554550,"outcome":"ai","attempts":2,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","verify_model":"claude-haiku-5-5","input_tokens":5834,"output_tokens":4037,"problems":[["beginner sentence 1 '今日の天気は良好です。' is unnatural in everyday Japanese; native speakers would say '今日の天気はいいです' or use 良好 only in forecast or report contexts. Its English 'Today's weather is excellent' also overstates 良好, which means good, favorable, or satisfactory rather than excellent.","definition_ja '物事の状態がとてもよいことを表します' overstates the meaning by putting 'とても' (very) before 'よい'. 良好 means the state is good or favorable, not necessarily very good, so the definition is somewhat misleading."]]}
